     "says": "Unsupported/supported walls: minimum 0.8 mm"
    },
    {
     "source": "https://www.hubs.com/knowledge-base/key-design-considerations-3d-printing/",
     "says": "All 3D printers can print walls thicker than 0.8 mm"
    },
    {
     "source": "https://help.prusa3d.com/article/modeling-with-3d-printing-in-mind_164135",
     "says": "0.4 mm nozzle: 1 perimeter = 0.45 mm, 2 perimeters = 0.9 mm; thinner than one perimeter is not printable"
    }
   ],
   "note": "0.45 mm is the single-perimeter floor for a 0.4 mm nozzle; 0.8 mm is the service-bureau minimum."
  },
  {
